---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, mailto } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Privacy policy';
const description = 'What this site collects, which is almost nothing, and the one third party that receives your IP address.';

const updated = new Date(SITE.policiesUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-US',
  { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---
<Base title={title} description={description} nav="privacy">
<section class="page-hero on-night">
  <div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true"><i class="b1"></i><i class="b2"></i><i class="b3"></i></div>
  <div class="container">
    <div>
      <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Privacy</li></ol>
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal · Updated {updated}</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">This site runs no analytics, sets no cookies, has no accounts and sends us nothing you type, so there is very little to describe. What follows is what actually happens when you load a page, not a template.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="narrow prose">
    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <p>We want to be specific, because "we value your privacy" means nothing. As of {updated}, this site:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>runs <b>no analytics</b> of any kind: no Google Analytics, no tag manager, no pixel, no third-party measurement script;</li>
      <li>sets <b>no cookies</b>, and writes nothing to local storage or session storage;</li>
      <li>has <b>no account system</b>, so there is nothing to sign up for and no password to store;</li>
      <li>sends us <b>nothing you type</b>. The search on the home page runs entirely in your browser: it matches what you type against the pages that already exist and navigates you to one. Nothing is submitted to us, and no third party is involved.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell, rent or share personal information, because we do not have any to sell.</p>

    <h2>What is unavoidable</h2>
    <h3>Server logs</h3>
    <p>The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare receives the IP address, user agent and requested URL of each request in order to deliver the page and to protect the site from abuse. We do not add analytics on top of that, and we do not build profiles from it.</p>
    <h3>Google Fonts</h3>
    <p>Page styling loads two typefaces from Google's font service (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>). That request goes to Google, which means <b>Google receives your IP address</b> when you load a page here. We gain nothing from this beyond the typeface, and we intend to serve the fonts from our own domain so that the transfer stops happening. Until then it is worth stating plainly rather than burying.</p>
    <h3>Links to law firm websites</h3>
    <p>Firm profiles link to each firm's own site. Once you follow such a link you are on that firm's site, subject to its privacy practices and not ours. We have no control over and take no responsibility for what a firm's site does with your data.</p>

    <h2>Information a firm sends us</h2>
    <p>If a firm writes to us to claim a profile, correct a value or appeal a score, we keep that correspondence and any documentation it contains for as long as needed to act on it and to show why a published value says what it says. That is business contact information and evidence, and we do not use it for marketing.</p>

    <h2>Information about firms and attorneys on this site</h2>
    <p>Profiles are compiled from sources the firm or a public body has published: the firm's own website, its Google Business Profile, state bar and court registries, court dockets, and third-party measurement services. Attorney names come from each firm's own published attorney pages, and every profile records where a value came from.</p>
    <p>If you are an attorney and believe something published about you is inaccurate, write to us and we will check it against the source and correct it if it is wrong. <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.</p>

    <h2>Your requests</h2>
    <p>You can ask what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Because we run no analytics and no accounts, in most cases the answer is that we hold nothing beyond what is described above. {SITE.email ? <>Write to <a href={mailto('Privacy request')}>{SITE.email}</a> with "Privacy request" as the subject.</> : <>Our contact channel is being set up; see <a href="/contact/">contact</a>.</>}</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 13.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes in a way that affects what we collect, the date at the top of this page changes with it. This version is dated {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
